From 92444e3701e61208583301f784a00cb0092e4b7f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 11:05:20 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Add admin dashboard: portfolio CMS, image upload, GA4
 analytics
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Replaces the non-functional Netlify CMS admin (git-gateway/Netlify
Identity doesn't work on Vercel hosting) with a self-contained admin
area at /admin, gated by a single-password session login:

- /api/admin/login, logout, me — HMAC-signed session cookie auth
- /api/portfolio — public GET, authenticated POST to replace the
  works list, backed by a Vercel Blob JSON store (falls back to the
  bundled data/portfolio.json seed if the blob doesn't exist yet)
- /api/admin/upload — image uploads to Vercel Blob (base64 JSON,
  capped ~3.5MB to stay under Vercel's request body limit)
- /api/admin/analytics — Google Analytics 4 Data API client using a
  service account (manual JWT signing, no googleapis dependency);
  degrades to a "not configured" state until GA_PROPERTY_ID,
  GA_CLIENT_EMAIL and GA_PRIVATE_KEY are set
- /admin/login.html, /admin/index.html — dashboard UI matching the
  site's dark glassmorphism theme: traffic charts/top pages/devices/
  countries, plus full works CRUD with drag-in image upload and
  gallery management
- portfolio.html now loads from /api/portfolio instead of the static
  JSON file directly, so admin edits go live without a code deploy
- ga4-tracking.js adds the GA4 gtag snippet to all public pages
  (inert placeholder ID until a real GA4 property is created)

Provisioned a Vercel Blob store and ADMIN_PASSWORD/SESSION_SECRET
env vars on the dson-site project to support this.
